e and coming back down use different numbers (a 5° gap, the deadband), so a noisy reading near a limit cannot make the state flicker." style="text;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#555555;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="235" width="1250" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="tilt" name="Tilt FSM – tilt servo (PB0)"><mxGraphModel dx="1200" dy="600" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1330" pageHeight="300" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="title" value="Tilt FSM – tilt servo (PB0)" style="text;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;html=1;fontSize=24;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#16124F;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1200" height="36" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="sub" value="tilt α = √(roll² + pitch²), in degrees. It is never negative." style="text;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;html=1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#555555;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="58" width="1200" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="start" value="" style="ellipse;shape=ellipse;perimeter=ellipsePerimeter;html=1;fillColor=#16124F;strokeColor=#16124F;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="143" width="24" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="b0" value="&lt;b&gt;FREE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;no force&lt;br&gt;tilt servo = 0°" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=16;fontColor=#222222;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="110" y="100" width="240" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="b1" value="&lt;b&gt;COMPLIANT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;early warning&lt;br&gt;tilt servo = 2 × α" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=